The plug-ins the tests load: where each comes from, its licence, and why it's here.

PICOH-101.wclap.tar.gz
    github.com/charCulbert/picoh-101 (MIT), synth/ built by tools/build-wclap.
    Shared imported memory, with the exports a second instance needs.

HeadlessGain.wclap.tar.gz
    github.com/charCulbert/char-clap-template (MIT), examples/effect-headless, an older build.
    The module's own memory, not shared; no interface.

Tapa.wclap.tar.gz
    github.com/charCulbert/Tapa, via github.com/charCulbert/char-wclaps: ISC in this build; MIT in later releases.
    Has presets. Built on the CLAP helpers, which check every call is on the thread CLAP requires.

HeavyMain.wclap.tar.gz
    heavy-main/ here (MIT), from char-clap-template; its third-party notices are in heavy-main/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
    Heavy main-thread work, for the threading tests.

Spawner.wasm
    spawner/ here (MIT), built by spawner/build.sh.
    Starts its own thread with pthread_create.

Not in the repo: `npm run fixtures` fetches these into .cache/, pinned by release or commit and sha256, and prints
each one's licence and source (test/fetch-fixture.ts lists them). A test fetches any it needs that's missing.
    - gui-lifecycle, process-lifecycle, probe and note-ids, from github.com/charCulbert/wclap-test-plugins v0.3.0 (MIT).
    - Twelve bundles built by github.com/andremichelle/open-webclap, each under its plug-in's own licence: Hive
      (CC0-1.0; the note sequencer the chain tests use), Note Lab, Pearls, Oxo Synth2 and WetChorus (MIT), and seven
      OpenRB-338 plug-ins (GPL-3.0-only). Their bundles' page files are open-webclap's MIT code.
